       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day under prescription dosing). A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common prescription anti-inflammatory regimen.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum daily dose.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), a typical analgesic regimen.\n- **1,600 mg total per day**, divided into doses.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and include a note with the clinical rationale. I can then enter it as written."
